From d6f19ab20f55b6c2e342d8d066d56804e4682e16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:27:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GTX 1660 / 6 GB: VRAM tier defaults, VICTORY_OUTPUT, FSR 1 at
 the present, presets

- vram_tier.rs: on a card whose budget is 6.5 GB or less (VICTORY_VRAM_TIER=auto|6gb|off)
  the card buffer copies (512 MB), texture copies (512 MB), room kept for render targets
  (2,304 MB), shader-visible card memory (768 MB) and texture staging (64 MB/frame) take
  the 6 GB values Protonida ran with; explicit settings still win.
- hooks.rs: VICTORY_OUTPUT=<w>x<h>, the title's output size (one of its modes), ported
  from deynesdev/Protonida; checked against the 1.0.2.1 hash and the bytes it replaces.
- host/fsr.rs: VICTORY_FSR=1, FSR 1 (EASU + RCAS after AMD's ffx_fsr1.h, MIT) at the
  present, to the screen's size (VICTORY_FSR_OUTPUT, VICTORY_FSR_SHARPNESS). On a
  Series S present only the world plane is enlarged; the interface is composed over it.
  Falls back to the compose pass's stretch if the host refuses the pipelines.
- scripts/play-gtx1660.ps1, Play-GTX1660.cmd: presets perf540 (540p -> 720p by the
  title's upscaler, FSR 1 to 1080p), test720, half (Series S at half scale), native.
- docs/GTX1660.ru.md. Not measured on a GTX 1660 yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WivgrhD8sETrePLpFesrny
